00:27:46.000 --> 00:28:13.000
My advice when I'm asked questions of this type is that you shouldn't think about it. Don't think about it. And I'll tell you why. You know, automatic human cognitions are not that different from, doing any other kind of complicated sequence of steps. And so if you were to, I mean, these days, there aren't a lot of, you know, automobiles with stick shift ignitions.
当我被问到这类问题时，我的建议是：你根本不应该去想它。别去想它。我来告诉你为什么。你知道，自动人类认知与进行任何其他类型的复杂步骤序列没有什么不同。因此，如果我们要——我的意思是，现在没有很多手动挡汽车了。

50
00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:35.000
But if you can cast your mind back to the days when that was far more common, if you, we've all had this experience of trying to drive a car when we're not familiar with that. And it's like you've got one foot on the clutch and you've got your hand moving and you end up stalling out in traffic. The same thing is going to happen if you overthink it. The best thing that you could do, the best advice I have is don't think about the impression
