you're making. Just go and be yourself and hope that you've been lucky enough to have the right face, voice, and manner that will line up with the job that you're trying to get or the person you're trying to impress. Because ultimately, if you overthink it, you're just going to, you're just going to follow a little bit on your face. How did you get interested in studying first impression? and snap judgments.
只需去做好你自己，并希望你足够幸运，拥有能够符合你试图得到的工作或你试图打动的人的面孔、声音和举止。因为归根结底，如果你想得太多，你只会——你只会有点把事情搞砸。你是如何对研究第一印象和瞬间判断产生兴趣的？

52
00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:38.000
When I was growing up, I was befuddled by things that I would see people do that contrasted with the things that they would say. And I grew up in an environment that was quite violent. There was a lot of crime. I grew up across the street from what we would have called a crack house at the time. They were not only dealing drugs, they were running prostitution and all of these things. And the altercations that would occur at a place like this would often spill over onto our property as well.
在我成长过程中，我被人们所做的事情与他们所说的话形成对比的现象搞糊涂了。我在一个相当暴力的环境中长大。那里有很多犯罪。我在当时我们称之为“瘾君子屋”的街对面长大。他们不仅在贩毒，还在经营卖淫以及所有这些事情。这种地方发生的冲突往往也会蔓延到我们的财产上。

53
00:29:38.000 --> 00:30:00.000
And so I needed to develop a high level of vigilance. And in those circumstances, I started to glean pretty quickly that the judgments that people would make based on very small amounts of information were guiding a lot of the things that they would do somewhat instinctively, habitually, and seemingly without a lot of depth of
因此，我需要培养高度的警惕性。在这种情况下，我开始很快地领会到，人们根据极少量信息做出的判断，在很大程度上指导了他们的许多行为——带有某种本能的、习惯性的，并且似乎缺乏很多深度的行为。

54
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:52.000
thought. And so based on that experience, I was extremely interested in understanding that dichotomy between, as I said, what people say and what they do. And so when I had the great privilege and opportunity of going away for a post-secondary education to college, I really wanted to study this as long as I could. I was the first person in my family to go away, to get an education and I didn't think I was going to be there very long. I expected that I would fail. And so I was I was really doggedly pursuing this right from the beginning because I figured I didn't have a great window of opportunity to get an answer to these questions. And so I started asking the questions, finding answers, going to the library, irritating my professors with lots
想法。所以基于那段经历，我非常渴望去理解这种二分法，正如我所说，人们说的和他们做的是两回事。因此，当我获得去大学接受高等教育的巨大特权和机会时，我真的很想尽可能长时间地研究它。我是家族中第一个离开家去求学的人，我当时并不认为自己能在那里呆多久。我预料自己会失败。所以从一开始我就一直在执着地追求这个方向，因为我觉得自己没有多少好机会来得到这些问题的答案。于是我开始提问、寻找答案、去图书馆、用大量问题去打扰我的教授们

