00:30:52.000 --> 00:31:24.000
of questions and professors at other universities as well. At one time, my first few weeks as a freshman in college, I wrote an email to Noam Chomsky asking him a question. He wrote back with a kind reply that, you know, in retrospect, I can see he was really humoring me. But I really wanted to pursue it, as I said, as long as I could. And even once I did manage to graduate and get into graduate school, I had that same mentality where I was just going to study this for as long as I could
还有其他大学的教授。有一次，在我上大学新生的前几周，我给诺姆·乔姆斯基写了一电子邮件向他提问。他回了一封亲切的信，你知道，现在回想起来，我能看出他当时其实是在迁就我。但我真的很想继续追求它，正如我所说，只要我能坚持多久就多久。甚至在我成功毕业并进入研究生院之后，我还是那种心态，只要能研究多久就研究多久

