to understand better. And so that was really the genesis of my interest in this work. And I can say how fortunate I am that I've been able to make a career out of answering a question that is meant so much to me, not just intellectually but personally as well. So looking ahead, what are the big questions that you still want to answer? What are some of the things you're working on right now? I'm really interested in understanding what it is that we don't know about ourselves. right? So again, these contradictions or, you know, hypocrisies you could even call them in people's behaviors, there's all this information that we have. You know, in studies in my lab and others have
以便更好地理解。所以这真的是我对这项工作产生兴趣的起源。我可以毫不夸张地说，我是多么幸运，能够以解答一个对我有着如此重大意义的问题为职业，这不仅在学术上，在个人层面上也是如此。那么展望未来，你仍然想解答的重大问题是什么？你现在正在研究的一些事情是什么？我非常想了解我们对自己究竟有哪些是不了解的，对吧？所以再次回到这些矛盾，或者说你甚至可以称之为人们行为中的虚伪，我们拥有所有这些信息。你知道，在我的实验室和其他人的研究中

